prompt.text:
Implement a new interval-normalization module with this exact API:

```ts
export interface IntegerSpan {
  start: number;
  end: number;
}

export function coalesceSpans(spans: readonly IntegerSpan[]): IntegerSpan[];
export function containsValue(spans: readonly IntegerSpan[], value: number): boolean;
```

Every endpoint and queried value must be a safe integer. A span with `start > end` is malformed. Throw `RangeError` for any malformed span or value. `coalesceSpans` must return new objects sorted by ascending `start`, then ascending `end`, merging spans that overlap or are directly adjacent. An empty input returns an empty array. It must not sort, mutate, or reuse any input object. `containsValue` accepts spans in any order, validates every span even if an earlier one contains the value, and returns whether the value lies within at least one inclusive span. It must not mutate its input.

Return only the complete source file; do not include Markdown fences or prose.

